   {"on": "with the usual leniency of the democracy", "text": "An interesting remark. The writer, no friend of extreme democracy, still notes that the Athenians let the tyrants' supporters stay. Ostracism was a mild weapon: exile for ten years, with property kept and no disgrace attached."},
   {"on": "any one who seemed to be more powerful than was expedient", "text": "Here is the danger in ostracism. It began as a guard against tyranny and became a way of removing anyone who stood out. Xanthippus, the first victim 'unconnected with the tyrants', was the father of Pericles."},
