 {"q": "Which is the fairest reply to 'Athens was not a democracy because women and slaves could not vote'?", "options": ["Women and metics could vote in the council, though not in the assembly", "It is true that most residents were excluded; what was new was that poor male citizens had equal power with the rich, and both facts should be held together", "Exclusions do not matter, because the assembly decided for everyone", "Athens was not a democracy at all, since only the rich held power"], "answer": 1, "why": "The exclusions were real and large; the inclusion of the poor was also real and without precedent."}
